course: dictionary
lesson: 190
title: Airless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Airless is built from air and -less, which means without. So airless means with no fresh air moving, or with no air at all. The word often shows up where a place feels stuffy, still or hard to breathe in.
explain: Look at the words around it. «An airless room» needs a window opened, because the air is stuffy. «The airless surface of the Moon» tells you there is no air there at all. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a room with no fresh air moving" fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Context also tells you which meaning to pick. In weather, airless means very still with no wind. In a story, an airless place often feels hot, heavy or scary. Check the nearby words before you decide.
fact: Airless means with no fresh air moving, or with no air at all.
fact: «An airless room» is stuffy and hard to breathe in.
fact: «The airless surface of the Moon» has no air, so there is no wind and no breathing without a spacesuit.
fact: Airless can also describe weather that is very still, with no wind.
fact: Peat bogs are cold, wet and airless, so dead plants there rot very slowly.
exercise: Mum says, «Open the window, this room is airless.» What does airless mean here? | Full of toys and games | Bright and sunny | Freezing cold, with snow outside | *Stuffy, with no fresh air moving
exercise: Why does the text call the surface of the Moon airless? | It is covered in trees and grass | *It has no air at all | It is covered in water | It is very noisy
exercise: «It was a still, airless day with no wind.» What does airless tell you about the day? | It was noisy and busy | It was full of bright sunshine | *It was very still, with no wind | It was cold and icy
test: What does airless mean? | Made of water and mud | Full of fresh, moving air | Very loud and noisy | *Without fresh air moving, or with no air at all
test: In which sentence does airless mean stuffy? | «The airless room made everyone feel tired.» | «The airless Moon has no sound.» | *«The window was open, so the room was not airless.» | «The airless day was full of wind.»
exam: In «the airless marsh mud», what does airless tell you about the mud? | It sits on top of a mountain | It is very loud and busy | *Bacteria work there without fresh air | It is full of bright sunlight
